{
  "id": "Compound::DB00208 - Gene::1559",
  "verbalization": "Ticlopidine is likely to interact with Cyp2c9 through a shared interaction with Cyp2c19, as evidenced by multiple paths indicating that Ticlopidine binds to Cyp2c19 and that Cyp2c19 participates in monooxygenase activities, which are catalyzed by Cyp2c9. The evidence suggests that Ticlopidine may inhibit Cyp2c9 by targeting Cyp2c19, which in turn affects the activity of Cyp2c9. The variation in the monooxygenase activities—whether (r)-limonene 6-monooxygenase or (s)-limonene 7-monooxygenase—indicates that Cyp2c19 may have multiple isoforms or that the activity is context-dependent, but the core mechanism of interaction between Ticlopidine and Cyp2c9 remains consistent. The integration of these paths highlights a potential regulatory relationship where Ticlopidine influences Cyp2c9 through a shared pathway involving Cyp2c19, emphasizing the role of Cyp2c9 in the metabolic activation of limonene derivatives.",
